<!--
  Hub home — the primary app's index route (`/`).

  The simplest possible page: a heading and a subheading. The template
  reads `{name()}` from the controller's scope, which triggers the
  compiler to emit a `hydrate()` function on the view's setup
  return — without any signal read, the runtime's mount() would have
  nothing to call (the compiler only emits hydrate when the template
  binds to scope signals). The signal is unused; the read is a no-op
  marker for the compiler.
-->
<main>
  <h1>{name()}</h1>
  <p>Ship's primary app — ready when you are.</p>
</main>
